Now let me understand the CUSD penalty formulas. Based on the contract model fields:

**PVEMA** (Penalidade por Volume Excedente na Medição Acima): penalty for exceeding upper transport tolerance
- When daily consumption > QDC × (1 + pvemaTolerancePercent/100)
- Penalty = excess volume × gas price (basePricePerUnit)

**PVEME** (Penalidade por Volume Excedente na Medição Excedente abaixo): penalty for falling below lower transport tolerance
- When daily consumption < QDC × (1 - pvemeTolerancePercent/100)
- Penalty = deficit volume × gas price

**Sobredemanda** (Overdemand): tiered formula for consumption exceeding QDC
- Tier 1: 0% to overdemandTier1MaxPercent (e.g., 110%) of QDC - no charge (within tolerance)
- Tier 2: overdemandTier1MaxPercent to overdemandTier2MaxPercent (e.g., 115%) of QDC - charged at overdemandTier2Multiplier × TUSD
- Tier 3: above overdemandTier2MaxPercent of QDC - charged at overdemandTier3Multiplier × TUSD

